<p>Have to agree with this. The main thing coming to my mind as an issue is that there is no real connection between the manifestations. Most seem to reflect the ink user's state of mind, but then there's the one that's suggested to be an image of the D-Class's victim. &quot;That's a bad mirror&quot; is a great line, but as psul said, has associated problems.</p>
<p>This also has the effect of making the description very bland. I'm reading about these things appearing behind a person and going, okay, what are they? Given that they're very individualized, the bulk of the description ends up in the testing logs; ergo, getting there faster is suggested.</p>
<p>You've also got some tone issues, like &quot;betray no awareness&quot; and &quot;numerous reports of insanity&quot; (or maybe it's just that I can't see that being a thing), and I had to look askance at them subjecting a D-Class to &quot;45 minutes of psychological torture&quot; just because. I mean, maybe it's because you used that exact phrase. The connection to the other SCPs linked in the article isn't apparent, and there's also what I said above, though at least these things are visible to others. (I would suggest dropping the lucid dream angle, since nothing is made of it, but I'm extremely biased against dream skips.)</p>

